@startuml
' A `while` with a `backward` action goes back on the right through it
' and out on the left, as PlantUML draws it; a note after `backward` is
' the body's last action's.
start
while (More pages?) is (yes)
  :Print a page;
  :Turn it over;
  (again) backward :Log the page; (next)
  note right: kept for the audit
endwhile (no)
:Done;
while (Printer busy?)
  backward :Wait;
endwhile
stop
@enduml
